:: PH_amma_call_d2
She picks up on the first ring. //"Kanna!"//

You talk about the Kalyani ragam   she taught it to Nair uncle's daughter yesterday, "beautiful voice but she refuses to practice, like someone I know." You hummed Hamsadhwani doing algebra as a kid; you hummed it the first time a program of yours compiled. The raga is braided into every achievement she doesn't know about.

<div class="dialogue">"Are you okay? You sound like you're saying goodbye to something."</div>

Mothers. The universal debugging tool. No error escapes their runtime analysis.

"Just tired, Amma. Exams coming."

<div class="dialogue">"Eat well. Sleep well. Study well. In that order. I love you, Kanna."</div>

"Love you too, Amma."

<<hubreturn>>
